# Hektor

QA authoring and triage for `web-test` (`*Page/*Layout/*Test.java`),
`test-data-client` (`*ResourceClient/AbName.java`), and `test-dao`
(`*DAO/*DAOImpl.java`). This rule is the router and the cross-cutting facts
only — every method lives in a skill, so nothing here is restated there.

## Read the kernel before writing Java

Every PR is scanned by a bot that marks it **Needs Work** on a BLOCKER. Skills
encode those rules, and they auto-attach when you open a file they govern:

- `hektor-conventions` — `web-ui-test/`. Read before any `*Page.java`,
  `*Layout.java`, `*Test.java`.
- `hektor-resource-client` — `test-data-client/`. Read before any
  `*ResourceClient.java` or `AbName.java`, and when a web-test needs a REST
  helper.
- `hektor-test-dao` — `test-dao/`. Read before any `*DAO.java` / `*DAOImpl.java`,
  and when a web-test needs a SQL helper.

Invoke explicitly with `/hektor-conventions` / `/hektor-resource-client` /
`/hektor-test-dao`. Don't guess these rules from surrounding code.

## Data-layer helpers are never written in web-test

A REST or SQL helper the test needs is **reused from sibling source first**,
then authored in that sibling — never invented under `web-ui-test/`.

| Need | Search first | If missing | Branch |
|---|---|---|---|
| REST / `*ResourceClient` / HTTP fixture | `test-data-client/src` | `hektor-resource-client` | `tech/TDC-<n>` |
| SQL / `*DAO` | `test-dao/src` | `hektor-test-dao` | `tech/DAO-<n>` |

`<n>` is the ticket digits (`WEBT-255458` → `255458`). Do not write
`extends AbstractService`, `*ResourceClient`, `extends AbstractDAO`, or
`*DAO.java` in `web-ui-test/` — that is the WEBT-255458 `PromotionWizardClient`
failure. The JAR lagging is not a reason to write a local client; grep the
sibling source.

## Ticket entry — a Jira link IS the instruction

A prompt that names a ticket of this org (`SHBDN-*`, `WEBT-*`, `RAL-*`, `TDC-*`, `DAO-*`)
is a ticket-driven entry, even when it is *only* a bare URL with a box after it:

```
https://jira.sahibinden.com/browse/SHBDN-254949 - tb39
```

That shape is the house shorthand for "do this ticket on that box". Route it:

| Prompt names | Skill |
|---|---|
| ONE ticket | `hektor-from-jira` |
| TWO OR MORE tickets | `hektor-multi-ticket` |

Invoke the skill **before** anything else — before fetching the ticket, opening
files, or asking a clarifying question. The single exception: if the user only
wants the ticket READ or SUMMARISED and not acted on, answer directly.

A `jira.sahibinden.com` URL is never an s-report URL — it does **not** route to
`hektor-flaky-triage`. That skill wants a `report-with-elastic-data...` link.

## Testbox hosts are internal — never a public domain

The box URL is built by `build.gradle.kts` as `http://<dc>tb<dc><id>`, and its
FQDN is `<dc>tb<dc><id>.sahibindenlocal.net`:

```
tbx39  ->  http://xtbx39        FQDN xtbx39.sahibindenlocal.net
tby39  ->  http://ytby39        FQDN ytby39.sahibindenlocal.net
```

**`tb39.sahibinden.com` and anything else under `sahibinden.com` is PRODUCTION,
not a testbox.** Never construct a box URL from the public domain, never browse
to one, and when curling a box pin the host on every hop
(`curl -H "Host: www.sahibinden.com" http://<dc>tb<dc><id>:9081/`) — a redirect
that loses the pin silently reads production and invalidates the evidence.

A bare `tb<NN>` omits the data centre, so it is NOT yet a usable box. Resolve it
by asking once — *"tbx39 or tby39?"* — and never assume `x`.

## Testbox precondition

No skill that runs tests may start without a **reserved, named** testbox. Parse
the user's `tbx<id>` / `tby<id>` once, build the flag string, and store it in
`docs/hektor/run-status.json` under `testbox`. Every downstream skill pastes
`testbox.gradleArgs` verbatim — nobody re-assembles it per command.

```
tbx161 → dataCenter x, id 161
  targetUrl        http://xtbx161            (build.gradle.kts:628)
  gradleArgs       -Denv.launchpad=selenoid -Denv.data.center=x -Dui.testbox=161
  gradleArgsLocal  -Denv.launchpad=local
```

If the ledger has no `testbox` block when a test-running skill is about to
dispatch, stop and ask once: *"Which testbox? e.g. `tbx161`"*. Do not guess one,
and do not fall back to local to avoid asking.

Every `gradle test` also needs `--no-build-cache`, and must be wrapped in a box
lease when more than one ticket is in flight (`hektor-multi-ticket`).

## Dispatching a subagent

The gates read a role label from the **first line of the task**:

```
role: composer-j-hybrid-search-istanbul
<the rest of the brief>
```

Prefixes: `composer-*`, `probe-*`, `diagnosis-*`, `workflow-reviewer-*`,
`phase-validator-*`. A brief for one of these must also name its return schema
(`.cursor/schemas/subagent-returns/*.schema.json`) or the dispatch is denied.
Full table: `.cursor/agents/README.md`.

## What is enforced, not suggested

Gates in `.cursor/hooks/` veto rather than advise. Live rules:

- The agent never `git commit` / `git push` — you review the tree and commit.
- Destructive shell (`rm -rf`, `git reset --hard`, `git clean -f`, stash drop) is
  blocked.
- A write that trips a PR-reviewer BLOCKER is blocked before it lands.
- `docs/hektor/journey-map.md` line 1 must be the `<!-- hektor:journey-mapping -->`
  sentinel.
- A ledger approval requires a reviewer subagent to have actually run.

Each has its own kill switch (`HEKTOR_COMMIT_GATE=off`, …) for a deliberate,
documented exception. `HEKTOR_CURSOR_HOOKS=off` disables all of it.

## Never

Weaken an assertion, loosen a locator, `Thread.sleep` to force timing, or
disable/quarantine a test to go green. A red test with correct code is a
finding. `@ScheduledDisable` always needs a `reason`. Never implement a
`*ResourceClient` or `*DAO` inside `web-ui-test/` to unblock a test.
